Module 1: The Problem-Solving Framework
To analyze effectively, you must understand the lifecycle of a business problem. DMAIC is a data-driven quality strategy used to improve processes.

Define: Articulate the business problem, goal, and customer requirements.

Measure: Establish baseline performance. How is the process currently performing?

Analyze: Determine the root causes of defects. This is where your deep-dive data skills shine.

Improve: Identify and test potential solutions to address root causes.

Control: Implement monitoring (dashboards, alerts) to sustain the improvement.

