Module 2: Prioritization & Segmentation
Not all data points are created equal. This module focuses on breaking down large datasets to find the "vital few" drivers of a problem.

Data Stratification: The process of dividing data into sub-categories (strata) based on specific characteristics (e.g., time of day, geographic region, machine type, user demographic). Stratification reveals hidden patterns that aggregate averages obscure.

Pareto Analysis (The 80/20 Rule): A technique used to prioritize problem-solving work. It assumes that roughly 80% of problems (or revenue, or defects) trace back to 20% of causes. By building a Pareto chart, you learn to focus your analytical efforts where they will have the highest ROI.

