Module 3: Performance Tracking
Dashboards often fail because they track the wrong things. Understanding the difference between indicator types is critical for business insights.

Lagging Indicators: Metrics that measure past performance. They are easy to measure but hard to change (e.g., Total Revenue, Customer Churn Rate, Total Defects Last Month). They tell you what happened.

Leading Indicators: Predictive metrics that signal future outcomes. They are harder to measure but easier to influence (e.g., Average Handle Time, System Uptime, Number of QA Training Hours Completed). They tell you what is going to happen.

