Module 4: Quality & Defect Analytics
To fix a broken process, you must know exactly how, where, and how often it breaks, and build systems to catch it before it fails again.

Defect Quantification: Sizing the problem. This involves counting the absolute number of defects and translating them into business impact (financial cost, hours lost, customer satisfaction drop).

Defect Opportunity Measurement: A more nuanced metric. A "defect" is a single failure, but an "opportunity" is any chance for a defect to occur. Calculating Defects Per Million Opportunities (DPMO) standardizes error rates across processes of varying complexity.

Proactive Control: Moving from reactive reporting to preventative analytics. This involves setting up Statistical Process Control (SPC) charts with Upper and Lower Control Limits to detect when a process is drifting out of variance before it generates massive defects.

