Practical Application Exam
To complete your upskilling, you must apply these concepts to the following business scenarios. Please draft your responses in a detailed analytical memo.

Scenario A: The Churn Crisis (DMAIC & Indicators)
Our primary SaaS product has seen a 15% increase in customer churn over the last quarter.

DMAIC Application: Outline the specific analytical steps you would take in the Measure and Analyze phases to investigate this issue. What data would you pull?

Indicator Design: "Quarterly Churn Rate" is a lagging indicator. Propose three leading indicators we should track on our executive dashboard to predict and prevent churn before the quarter ends.

Scenario B: Call Center Overload (Stratification & Pareto)
Customer Support is receiving an unmanageable volume of refund requests. You are given a dataset containing 50,000 refund tickets from the past month.

Stratification: Identify at least four different variables you would use to stratify this data to find meaningful patterns.

Pareto Execution: Assume you categorized the reasons for refunds. The top three reasons account for 78% of the volume, while the remaining twelve reasons account for 22%. Explain how you would present this finding to the VP of Operations and what your strategic recommendation would be.

Scenario C: Manufacturing Quality (Defects & Proactive Control)
You are analyzing a smartphone assembly line. A phone has 45 distinct parts, meaning there are 45 opportunities for a defect per unit. Last week, the line produced 10,000 phones and QA found 180 total defects.

Defect Opportunity Measurement: Calculate the DPMO (Defects Per Million Opportunities) for this assembly line. Show your formula.

Proactive Control: How would you design a proactive control system for this assembly line using data? Describe the alerting mechanism you would put in place to ensure the line stops before producing another 180 defects next week.
